I think you misunderstood Raisse.

What she probably meant was that once you discover a bones level, the 
corpse there starts rotting, but the moment you discover the level is 
counted as the moment at which the death occurs.

So if you enter a level and immediately happen upon the grave, the 
corpse laying there will count as freshly killed. However, if you find a 
bones level, leave it immediately, and come back later, the corpse 
*will* have rotted.

